  "correction": "Recursive ternary majority at depth m has I=(3/2)^m, H=4(I-1), and C_occ>=(m-4)I+4, so C_occ/I diverges and every fixed-lambda finite-center reserve fails. Independently, B01 antipodal two-flip dictators have K_occ>=(n-8)(I-1), refuting the same architecture near I=1. The refutation concerns only a fixed lambda>0 universal reserve at finite center. Lambda=0, nonlinear or state-dependent credit use, signed identities, phase monotonicity and FEI are not refuted. The sparse every-root-block conclusion separately requires elementary-child validity.",
